      "questionText": "A farmer is cultivating 2 hectares of transplanted semi-dwarf rice (target yield 6 t/ha). The soil test recommendation is 120 kg N, 60 kg P2O5, and 40 kg K2O per hectare. Calculate: (1) Total quantity of Urea (46% N), Single Super Phosphate (16% P2O5), and Muriate of Potash (60% K2O) required for the entire 2 hectares, and (2) Detail the exact split application schedule for nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium across crop growth stages.",
      "modelAnswer": "STEP-BY-STEP FERTILIZER CALCULATIONS AND SCHEDULING:\n\n1. TOTAL FERTILIZER QUANTITY COMPUTATION (FOR 2 HECTARES):\n\nA. Single Super Phosphate (SSP - 16% P2O5):\n- Recommended $P_2O_5$ per ha = 60 kg\n- Total $P_2O_5$ for 2 ha = $60 \\times 2 = 120 \\text{ kg}$\n- Quantity of SSP required:\n  $$\\text{SSP} = \\frac{120 \\times 100}{16} = 750 \\text{ kg (or 15 bags of 50 kg)}$$\n\nB. Muriate of Potash (MOP - 60% K2O):\n- Recommended $K_2O$ per ha = 40 kg\n- Total $K_2O$ for 2 ha = $40 \\times 2 = 80 \\text{ kg}$\n- Quantity of MOP required:\n  $$\\text{MOP} = \\frac{80 \\times 100}{60} = 133.33 \\text{ kg (or 2.67 bags of 50 kg)}$$\n\nC. Urea (46% N):\n- Recommended N per ha = 120 kg\n- Total N for 2 ha = $120 \\times 2 = 240 \\text{ kg}$\n- Quantity of Urea required:\n  $$\\text{Urea} = \\frac{240 \\times 100}{46} = 521.74 \\text{ kg (or 11.6 bags of 45 kg)}$$\n\n2. PRECISION SPLIT APPLICATION SCHEDULE:\n\n- Basal Application (At Final Puddling before Transplanting):\n  - 100% of Phosphorus (750 kg SSP) is incorporated into the mud, as phosphorus is immobile and critical for early root elongation.\n  - 75% of Potassium (100 kg MOP) is incorporated to promote early stem strength.\n  - 25% of Nitrogen (130 kg Urea) is applied as basal dressing into the reduced soil layer.\n  - Additionally, broadcast 50 kg Zinc Sulphate ($ZnSO_4 \\cdot 7H_2O$) to prevent Khaira disease.\n\n- First Top-Dressing at Active Tillering (21-25 Days After Transplanting - DAT):\n  - 35% of Nitrogen (182 kg Urea) is broadcast. Drain excess standing water prior to application and re-flood 24 hours later to minimize volatilization.\n\n- Second Top-Dressing at Panicle Initiation Stage (45-50 DAT):\n  - 30% of Nitrogen (157 kg Urea) is applied to maximize the number of spikelets per panicle.\n  - Remaining 25% of Potassium (33.3 kg MOP) is applied here to boost grain filling and disease resistance.\n\n- Third Top-Dressing at Heading / Booting Stage (Optional, guided by LCC):\n  - Remaining 10% of Nitrogen (52 kg Urea) is applied only if the Leaf Color Chart (LCC) reads below panel score 4, ensuring green flag leaves during milking.",
      "outlinePoints": [
        "Step 1: Fertilizer conversion calculations for 2 hectares (750 kg SSP, 133.3 kg MOP, 521.7 kg Urea)",
        "Basal dressing: 100% P, 75% K, 25% N, and ZnSO4 incorporated during final puddling",
        "First split: 35% N at active tillering (21 DAT) with water management",
        "Second split: 30% N + 25% K at panicle initiation (45 DAT) for spikelet fertility",
        "Third split: 10% N at heading stage guided by Leaf Color Chart"
      ]
